@startuml local_control_dispatch
title Persisted Control Dispatch to the Original Runtime
' Contract baseline: pi-mono-java-design 2ee2a3211da68ad87b0d9cab353e691b00bdaebd
' Java baseline: 1af21fd574817a7c18a48d05cc8975b4d3a98766
' Implementation: 6a66f5b8c65e1cd112f790f79817a4ac381391c3
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/ExecutionControlPollingService.java#poll
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionControlDispatcher.java#dispatchStop and dispatchConfirmation
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java#activeTargets
' Pi source: packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts#runAgentLoop and prepareToolCall at 4af9d21d3b4d664e4a29fcabfec85171077248e3
' Observed behavior: the original Java holder owns the agent, credentials, and pending confirmation future.
' Design reason: database signals must be applied only to the exact in-memory execution.
' Java divergence: fixed cross-process targets and polling are CampusClaw architecture changes.
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
database "Persistent control store" as store
component "Control polling service" as poller
interface "RuntimeLocalControlDispatcher" as port
component "RuntimeSessionControlDispatcher" as dispatcher
component "RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry" as registry
component "RuntimeActiveExecution" as execution
component "Original Agent and credentials" as agent

registry --> poller : bounded active targets
store --> poller : pending stop or confirmation
poller --> port : dispatch exact target
dispatcher -up-|> port
dispatcher --> registry : session operation lock
registry --> execution : exact fixed target
execution --> agent : abort signal or resume future
dispatcher --> store : claim and acknowledge decision

note right of execution
The holder remains local.
Credentials never enter the control store.
end note
@enduml
